<title>USA: BankBoston taps global derivative director.</title>
<headline>BankBoston taps global derivative director.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>BankBoston Corp said on Wednesday that it has appointed Robert Scott as managing director of its global derivatives sales.</p>
<p>BankBoston said Scott most recently was a senior vice president at Lehman Brothers in New York, responsible for structuring derivative transactions for high yield clients as well as for cross-border merger and acquisition deals.</p>
<p>The bank said Scott has been active in the derivatives market since 1985.</p>
